# Authoring

## Frontmatter

Every page carries a `description` — it feeds search results and is how
AI agents decide whether a page is relevant without reading all of it.
Order pages with `sidebar_position`; the sidebar itself mirrors the
`docs/` folder structure.

## Diagrams

Mermaid fences render to SVG **at build time** — readers never wait on a
JavaScript renderer, and the diagram source stays in the page for agents:

```mermaid
graph LR
  Author -- "writes mermaid" --> Build
  Build -- "ships SVG + source" --> Readers
  Build -- "ships SVG + source" --> Agents
```

A syntax error in any fence fails the build with the file, line, and a
caret pointing at the problem — fix the diagram and rebuild. There is no
"broken diagram in production" state.

## Theme

The color theme is compiled from `branding.brandColor` in
`docusaurus.config.ts` — including the dark mode palette, which is
derived *lighter* than the brand color so text stays readable. Don't
hand-write `--ifm-color-primary` CSS variables.
